That framing makes sense psychologically: the “dream” is the inherited model you mistake for reality.

Waking up is noticing the separation between the story about you and the thing doing the noticing. Once you can see the script as a script, it loses some automatic authority. Then identity becomes less like a verdict and more like a model you can inspect, revise, and choose how much to obey.

In Pantheon terms, it’s a model/observer split:

assigned identity → embodied repetition → unconscious fusion → recognition of the model → observer regains leverage → deliberate re-authorship

The important part is that waking up doesn’t require proving the old story was entirely false. It only requires realizing it was constructed. Constructed things can be edited.